{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 15:44:19.352531", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Health Assessment:\\nThe network appears to have significant connectivity issues. Based on the reachability test results, many hosts are unable to communicate with each other. This is particularly concerning given the scalable SDN spine-leaf topology, which is designed to ensure robust connectivity between all hosts and switches.\\n\\n#### Observations:\\n1. **Reachability Results:**\\n   - **Host-to-Host Communication:**\\n     - Host `host_1_2` successfully communicated with `host_1_1` with no packet loss and reasonable RTT values (average RTT: 31.186 ms).\\n     - Host `host_1_3` successfully communicated with `host_1_1` with no packet loss, but the RTT values were higher (average RTT: 57.18 ms).\\n     - All other host-to-host communication attempts either failed or returned an \"unknown\" status, indicating no response or incomplete tests.\\n\\n   - **Inter-Subnet Communication:**\\n     - Hosts from other subnets (e.g., `host_2_1`, `host_3_1`, `host_4_1`) failed to communicate with hosts in subnet `10.0.0.0/24`. This suggests potential issues with routing or switch configurations.\\n\\n2. **Status Summary:**\\n   - Out of the tested host pairs, only two pairs (`host_1_2` to `host_1_1` and `host_1_3` to `host_1_1`) showed successful communication.\\n   - The majority of tests resulted in \"unknown\" statuses, indicating widespread connectivity problems.\\n\\n#### Relevant Findings:\\n- **Local Connectivity:** Hosts within the same subnet (`10.0.0.0/24`) show partial connectivity, with some hosts able to communicate successfully while others fail.\\n- **Global Connectivity:** Hosts across different subnets are unable to communicate, which could point to issues with the spine-leaf topology, OpenFlow controller, or routing configurations.\\n- **RTT Variability:** The RTT values for successful communications vary significantly, which may indicate congestion or suboptimal routing paths.\\n\\n#### Next Steps:\\nFurther investigation is required to pinpoint the root cause of these connectivity issues. This will involve examining the configurations of the switches, the OpenFlow controller, and the routing tables. Additionally, testing the management network (20.0.0.0/24) and verifying the SDN controller\\'s functionality will be crucial.\\n\\nThis report highlights the abnormal behavior in the network and provides a foundation for deeper analysis., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='494b8c28-1aa7-41df-b17e-a1405a3d5ca8'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
